 (A) Introduction. Certain noise levels must be tolerated by all citizens in order for the normal functions of city life to continue; however, excessive noise is detrimental to the physical, mental and social well being of the citizens of the city as well as to their comfort, living conditions, general welfare and safety ... , any loud, unnecessary, or unusual noise that is excessive, disruptive and/or annoying is ... to regulation as provided
